"cbb2325005c8d8665412":{"version":"Text considered: The King in All His Beauty (published lyrics). Artist/publisher text; the exact stanza selection and recording remain for human verification. This report concerns the catalog text, independently of personal or imported assessments.","summary":"A preliminary AI reading of doctrinal accuracy, theological substance, and language, with separate catalog text scores. The reasons explain these provisional scores, not your personal or imported judgments. No church-use decision is made.","reasons":[{"criterion":"Doctrinal accuracy","explanation":"The heavenly Holy One becomes the substitute for sinners and the reigning Lamb. Christ's humiliation and exaltation together explain his worth."},{"criterion":"Theological substance","explanation":"Divine majesty, substitutionary atonement, resurrection glory and worldwide worship supply rich gospel content across the three scenes."},{"criterion":"Language & craftsmanship","explanation":"Heavenly throne, thorn crown and glorious Lamb give beauty a concrete saving meaning. The repeated worthy confession is supported rather than merely asserted."}],"scores":{"accuracy":9,"substance":9,"language":9,"time":null},"quote":"","concerns":[],"themes":["Christ's worth","Substitutionary atonement","Heavenly worship"],"scriptures":[{"reference":"Isaiah 6:1","quote":"In the year that king Uzziah died I saw also the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's worth, substitutionary atonement, heavenly worship. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"1 Peter 3:18","quote":"For Christ also hath once suffered for sins, the just for the unjust, that he might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh, but quickened by the Spirit:","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's worth, substitutionary atonement, heavenly worship. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Revelation 5:12","quote":"Saying with a loud voice, Worthy is the Lamb that was slain to receive power, and riches, and wisdom, and strength, and honour, and glory, and blessing.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's worth, substitutionary atonement, heavenly worship. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"}],"source":{"url":"https://sovereigngracemusic.com/music/songs/the-king-in-all-his-beauty/","label":"The King in All His Beauty (published lyrics) · Matt Boswell & Matt Papa · source transcription","kind":"artist-publisher-page","checkedAt":"2026-10-19","hash":"e22fcec1b728cca4c942bec8ff076f4162b41fff3d8462afcc6ed05322537650"},"limits":["The supplied transcription may omit, alter or misattribute a stanza. Compare it with your selected text before using the assessment.","Artist association does not verify a specific recording. No tempo, key, duration, arrangement or instrumental quality was inferred.","Human judgments, saved concerns, personal themes, recordings, approvals, libraries and plans are unchanged.","A supporting Scripture comparison is distinct from a verified quotation or deliberate allusion in the song."]},
