"fb1bcfe97bb30d213d23":{"version":"Text considered: Jesus, My Great High Priest (Hymnary representative text). Published hymn transcription; the exact stanza selection and recording remain for human verification. This report concerns the catalog text, independently of personal or imported assessments.","summary":"A preliminary AI reading of doctrinal accuracy, theological substance, and language, with separate catalog text scores. The reasons explain these provisional scores, not your personal or imported judgments. No church-use decision is made.","reasons":[{"criterion":"Doctrinal accuracy","explanation":"Christ's once-offered blood, substitution and continuing advocacy fully answer guilt. No additional sacrifice is sought for the conscience."},{"criterion":"Theological substance","explanation":"Atonement, fulfilled law, intercession, freedom from accusation and guarding grace provide exceptional concentration of saving doctrine."},{"criterion":"Language & craftsmanship","explanation":"Debt, courtroom defense and priestly blood form compatible explanations of assurance. The Father's gracious hearing is united with the Son's effective advocacy."}],"scores":{"accuracy":9,"substance":9,"language":9,"time":null},"quote":"","concerns":[],"themes":["Christ's priesthood","Atonement","Assurance"],"scriptures":[{"reference":"Hebrews 10:12","quote":"But this man, after he had offered one sacrifice for sins for ever, sat down on the right hand of God;","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's priesthood, atonement, assurance. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Hebrews 7:25","quote":"Wherefore he is able also to save them to the uttermost that come unto God by him, seeing he ever liveth to make intercession for them.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's priesthood, atonement, assurance. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Romans 8:34","quote":"Who is he that condemneth? It is Christ that died, yea rather, that is risen again, who is even at the right hand of God, who also maketh intercession for us.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of christ's priesthood, atonement, assurance. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"}],"source":{"url":"https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_my_great_high_priest","label":"Jesus, My Great High Priest (Hymnary representative text) · Isaac Watts · source transcription","kind":"published-hymnal","checkedAt":"2026-10-19","hash":"0e0b5f82b30bd752f85cd7915821daf3f813a5a515a5e7eab14963ba5648df0a"},"limits":["The supplied transcription may omit, alter or misattribute a stanza. Compare it with your selected text before using the assessment.","Artist association does not verify a specific recording. No tempo, key, duration, arrangement or instrumental quality was inferred.","Human judgments, saved concerns, personal themes, recordings, approvals, libraries and plans are unchanged.","A supporting Scripture comparison is distinct from a verified quotation or deliberate allusion in the song."]},
