"6ed12f1376881ea2be3b":{"version":"Text considered: Grace Greater than Our Sin. Published hymn transcription; the exact stanza selection and recording remain for human verification. This report concerns the catalog text, independently of personal or imported assessments.","summary":"A preliminary AI reading of doctrinal accuracy, theological substance, and language, with separate catalog text scores. The reasons explain these provisional scores, not your personal or imported judgments. No church-use decision is made.","reasons":[{"criterion":"Doctrinal accuracy","explanation":"Grace is presented as sufficient to pardon and cleanse actual guilt, not as a denial that sin matters."},{"criterion":"Theological substance","explanation":"The contrast between widespread sin and greater grace develops a clear account of pardon and the invitation to receive it."},{"criterion":"Language & craftsmanship","explanation":"The repeated comparison is coherent; the larger-than image concerns grace's sufficiency, not a measurable quantity or permission to continue in sin."}],"scores":{"accuracy":9,"substance":8,"language":8,"time":null},"quote":"","concerns":[],"themes":["Grace","Forgiveness","Cleansing"],"scriptures":[{"reference":"Romans 5:20","quote":"Moreover the law entered, that the offence might abound. But where sin abounded, grace did much more abound:","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of grace, forgiveness, cleansing. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"1 John 1:9","quote":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of grace, forgiveness, cleansing. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"}],"source":{"url":"https://github.com/ChurchApps/WorshipCommonsContent/blob/d3362e1d7c7f4d3f98b9310bb07aa480453508c7/songs/en/grace-greater-than-our-sin-L70IA21K2WO/sources/lyrics.chordpro","label":"Grace Greater than Our Sin · Julia Johnston & Daniel Towner · source transcription","kind":"published-hymnal","checkedAt":"2026-10-17","hash":"f0cd257cfbedb3adb2d422e1803b37049a4d4688aef503b71f4bb38f15544a68"},"limits":["The supplied transcription may omit, alter or misattribute a stanza. Compare it with your selected text before using the assessment.","Artist association does not verify a specific recording. No tempo, key, duration, arrangement or instrumental quality was inferred.","Human judgments, saved concerns, personal themes, recordings, approvals, libraries and plans are unchanged.","A supporting Scripture comparison is distinct from a verified quotation or deliberate allusion in the song."]},
